# Read by BOTH hosts while the move to Cloudflare is in progress, so it has to
# stay valid for each.
#
# Netlify: these are the live rules. netlify.toml carries the same ones, but
# this file wins, so a rule missing here is a route that 404s — that is exactly
# how /api/lab/health returned the SPA instead of JSON.
#
# Cloudflare: this file is honoured too, but wrangler.toml sets
# run_worker_first for /api/*, and that runs before any asset logic. So the
# Netlify function rule below never applies there — the Worker answers first.
# The catch-all is correct on both.
#
# Order matters: the SPA catch-all is last, or it would swallow the API paths
# and answer them with index.html.

/api/lab/chat      /.netlify/functions/lab-chat      200
/api/lab/health    /.netlify/functions/lab-health    200
/api/lab/settings  /.netlify/functions/lab-settings  200
/admin             /.netlify/functions/lab-admin     200
/*                 /index.html                       200
